1
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,346
[speaker clicks on]

2
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:18,768
I know this is a big change,
but change can be good.

3
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:20,437
Right?

4
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:22,063
[boat creaks]

5
00:00:25,483 --> 00:00:28,111
Yeah, this is going great. Cool.

6
00:00:28,194 --> 00:00:29,320
Ready… Row!

7
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:30,363
Wait, what?

8
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:32,657
-[rower] Whoa, not ready, not ready!
-[rower 2] Starting?

9
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:35,326
["Whiplash" by Aespa playing]

10
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:37,078
[grunts]

11
00:00:39,164 --> 00:00:40,832
Hey, we're lopsided.

12
00:00:40,915 --> 00:00:44,377
-Okay, port! More power!
-Are you sure?

13
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:45,420
Uh… uh…

14
00:00:45,503 --> 00:00:49,674
Sorry, starboard, more power.
Sorry, I'm used to facing the other way.

15
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:50,800
[Ryder] Port or starboard?

16
00:00:50,884 --> 00:00:52,343
-Rate's too high!
-Uh…

17
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:54,387
-It's starboard!
-[Josh] Baloo, slow down.

18
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:55,638
He's rushing the slide!

19
00:00:55,722 --> 00:00:57,557
-Okay, I know!
-Do you?

20
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:58,850
Baloo!

21
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:00,769
-Baloo, take it down!
-Trying!

22
00:01:00,852 --> 00:01:03,730
-[Josh] Ratio!
-Okay! Wean off!

23
00:01:03,813 --> 00:01:05,148
Ow!

24
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:06,858
Why're we stopping?

25
00:01:11,321 --> 00:01:14,365
Hey, we kept the receipt, right?
We can still send her back?

26
00:01:16,201 --> 00:01:17,494
Ha, ha, ha.

27
00:01:18,286 --> 00:01:20,163
<i>♪ Whip, whiplash ♪</i>

28
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:21,623
<i>♪ Whip, whiplash ♪</i>

29
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:23,500
<i>♪ Whip, whiplash ♪</i>

30
00:01:23,583 --> 00:01:25,168
<i>♪ One more, give 'em whiplash ♪</i>

31
00:01:25,251 --> 00:01:26,836
[school bell ringing]

32
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,463
[Cabrera] To avoid Teagan's dismissal,

33
00:01:28,546 --> 00:01:31,299
we can extend
a ten-day grace before payment.

34
00:01:31,382 --> 00:01:33,426
-I trust that'll suffice.
-[laughs]

35
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:34,969
Ten whole days.

36
00:01:35,053 --> 00:01:37,555
{\an8}Is there a problem, Mrs. Tao?
Or is it Emerson?

37
00:01:37,639 --> 00:01:39,099
{\an8}I go by Emerson now.

38
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:43,019
{\an8}Look, the education trust
has been implicated and seized,

39
00:01:43,103 --> 00:01:46,564
{\an8}and I really don't want to have
to pull Teagan out of another school.

40
00:01:46,648 --> 00:01:47,899
{\an8}If there's anything we could do…

41
00:01:47,982 --> 00:01:50,944
{\an8}Unfortunately, we've allocated
our financial aid for the year.

42
00:01:51,528 --> 00:01:54,697
{\an8}But we could set up an installment plan.

43
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:56,241
{\an8}Would $7,000 each month work?

44
00:01:56,324 --> 00:02:00,328
{\an8}Well, that's… very generous.

45
00:02:00,912 --> 00:02:02,288
Seems so doable.

46
00:02:02,372 --> 00:02:05,583
Otherwise, there are
family-funded scholarships,

47
00:02:05,667 --> 00:02:11,089
such as the Chou Scholarship,
awarded to students who the families feel

48
00:02:11,172 --> 00:02:14,551
belong to the Easton community
and represent its values.

49
00:02:15,552 --> 00:02:16,553
Ah.

50
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:19,013
Installment plan it is, then.

51
00:02:19,097 --> 00:02:20,223
[knocking on door]

52
00:02:20,306 --> 00:02:23,768
I assume you will be
at parents' night tonight.

53
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:27,856
Next Monday,
we'll get this tuition plan sorted.

54
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:28,940
[Ella] Okay.

55
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:32,735
Teagan's friend. What are you doing here?

56
00:02:32,819 --> 00:02:34,404
She set fire to a car.

57
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:38,283
It's my car. I can do what I want with it.

58
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,370
-Did my parents call?
-No.

59
00:02:43,079 --> 00:02:46,124
They'll take a jet to space,
but not Massachusetts.

60
00:02:51,504 --> 00:02:53,631
[Josh] Okay, boys, keep heading up.

61
00:02:54,757 --> 00:02:55,967
A little to the left.

62
00:02:57,302 --> 00:02:58,845
Ready, and down.

63
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:00,930
[Quaid] Worst practice ever.

64
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:03,308
-[Baloo] Not the worst.
-[Josh] Speak for yourself.

65
00:03:03,391 --> 00:03:06,394
You didn't lose a kidney because
the cox doesn't know her left from right.

66
00:03:06,477 --> 00:03:08,021
Looks like that hurts.

67
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:09,355
Watch yourself, Faid.

68
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:11,816
Hey, I'm not sure why you're arguing
who sucked most.

69
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:13,568
It was a nine-way tie.

70
00:03:13,651 --> 00:03:16,070
Not like we have a big race
or anything tomorrow.

71
00:03:16,738 --> 00:03:18,698
-What race?
-Line it up, boys.

72
00:03:18,781 --> 00:03:21,701
Come get your special event unis
for the alumni race.

73
00:03:21,784 --> 00:03:23,411
It's Easton Spirit Week.

74
00:03:23,494 --> 00:03:26,080
Every team has their event
leading into the Iron Crucible.

75
00:03:26,164 --> 00:03:28,541
-The school-wide obstacle course.
-It's designed to kill you.

76
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:30,752
Wrong! It is designed
to build perseverance.

77
00:03:30,835 --> 00:03:33,755
Legend says that in the last 100 years,
seven people have died.

78
00:03:33,838 --> 00:03:38,134
Statistically, that's only
a 0.07% chance of death.

79
00:03:38,218 --> 00:03:40,053
Our main event is the alumni race.

80
00:03:40,136 --> 00:03:42,805
The old crew come back
and race the new team.

81
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:44,265
It's the passing of the torch.

82
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:47,185
Unless they beat us.
Then it's more of a handing us our asses.

83
00:03:47,268 --> 00:03:51,147
So it's just a bunch of old dudes trying
to prove that they're still young and fit.

84
00:03:51,231 --> 00:03:53,608
They're probably all
one steak away from a heart attack.

85
00:03:53,691 --> 00:03:54,651
[laughing]

86
00:03:55,485 --> 00:03:59,197
Actually, it's our dads.
And mine's an Olympian.

87
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,865
And mine's a world-record holder.

88
00:04:01,449 --> 00:04:03,201
[laughs] We're going to get smoked.

89
00:04:04,535 --> 00:04:07,497
-So glad my moms don't row.
-I don't want Dad to have a heart attack.

90
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:11,334
Okay, boys. Let's get the boat away.

91
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:19,217
Uh, hey, guys, has anyone seen my cox box?

92
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,052
-Your cox what?
-[Noah] What's missing?

93
00:04:21,135 --> 00:04:22,345
-What?
-[Quaid] Saucy.

94
00:04:23,554 --> 00:04:26,891
You know what it is.
The amplifier, the microphone thing--

95
00:04:26,975 --> 00:04:30,853
Hands on the boat! Ready, up to shoulders.

96
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:32,605
And walk her in.

97
00:04:37,986 --> 00:04:41,155
Hey, El. Doing the lunch rush
take you back?

98
00:04:41,239 --> 00:04:44,075
Like I was 17 again. With shin splints.

99
00:04:44,701 --> 00:04:46,494
I got your tips from the other night.

100
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:50,540
Don't spend it all in one place,
unless that place is here.

101
00:04:50,623 --> 00:04:52,542
Hey, Jim, um…

102
00:04:54,085 --> 00:04:57,338
Any chance you'd flip me an advance
for my next check?

103
00:04:57,839 --> 00:05:01,426
It's for Teagan's school. I wouldn't ask
if you weren't my last resort.

104
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:04,804
I can front you a couple hundred.
Would that cover it?

105
00:05:05,847 --> 00:05:07,849
God, no. [laughs]

106
00:05:07,932 --> 00:05:09,517
But every little bit helps.

107
00:05:10,018 --> 00:05:11,436
Thanks, Jim.

108
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:12,603
Hang in there, kid.

109
00:05:13,479 --> 00:05:14,564
[exhales]

110
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:17,358
Ugh, where is it?

111
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:29,329
{\an8}Harder than it looks, huh?

112
00:05:31,122 --> 00:05:34,000
Yeah, getting eight boys to do anything
is impossible.

113
00:05:34,083 --> 00:05:37,045
That's the job of a coxswain.
You gotta get them to follow you.

114
00:05:37,545 --> 00:05:38,796
How?

115
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:43,092
You have to win minds and hearts.
Figure out what motivates them.

116
00:05:43,926 --> 00:05:48,097
Look, you're, um… You're like a conductor.
You're not a musician.

117
00:05:48,598 --> 00:05:50,850
You'll know soon enough
if coxing is for you or not.

118
00:05:51,351 --> 00:05:54,020
Just like Baloo's learning
he's not for stroke seat.

119
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:56,773
Come on.

120
00:05:59,025 --> 00:06:02,820
When the old boathouse burned down,
I thought it could use an upgrade.

121
00:06:02,904 --> 00:06:04,864
This is all reclaimed wood.

122
00:06:05,823 --> 00:06:07,450
There we are.

123
00:06:07,533 --> 00:06:10,828
You know, I was the fourth Regis
to row in the stroke seat.

124
00:06:11,329 --> 00:06:13,706
With my boy Josh in stroke,
he'll be the fifth.

125
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:14,874
Hm.

126
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:17,085
-Rich.
-Matt.

127
00:06:17,168 --> 00:06:20,213
I was just showing
some of the other alums my boathouse.

128
00:06:20,296 --> 00:06:21,422
Your boathouse?

129
00:06:21,506 --> 00:06:23,049
Well, donated.

130
00:06:23,132 --> 00:06:24,967
-Ah.
-This is Matt.

131
00:06:25,051 --> 00:06:26,386
We were stern pair,

132
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:28,513
-the seven to my eight.
-Mm.

133
00:06:28,596 --> 00:06:31,891
Even though he's coaching our competition,
he'll be in our boat tomorrow.

134
00:06:31,974 --> 00:06:34,977
And how are we feeling
about our alumni team's chances?

135
00:06:35,061 --> 00:06:37,980
-We've put our time in on the erg, right?
-[man] Sure have.

136
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:40,274
I hope your boys can give us
a run for our money.

137
00:06:40,358 --> 00:06:43,361
Oh, they'll put up a fight. Don't worry.

138
00:06:44,904 --> 00:06:48,116
-[Josh] Oh, way to choke in eight seat.
-[Baloo] Learned from the best.

139
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:50,701
[Baloo chuckles]

140
00:06:50,785 --> 00:06:52,245
We'll lose the flop.

141
00:06:52,745 --> 00:06:55,873
I wish Coach'd quit the character building
bullshit and put me back in.

142
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:58,292
I dunno, maybe Coach is looking
for other options in stroke.

143
00:06:58,376 --> 00:07:00,211
[laughs] Like who?

144
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:03,840
You?

145
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:06,259
-[tense music playing]
-Why not me?

146
00:07:06,342 --> 00:07:08,094
Yeah, sure.

147
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:10,221
I guess.

148
00:07:30,616 --> 00:07:32,618
-Dad!
-[Richard Regis] There's the stroke seat.

149
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:36,622
How was practice?
You, uh, keeping the crew in rhythm?

150
00:07:37,248 --> 00:07:39,333
-Yeah, getting there.
-Good.

151
00:07:39,417 --> 00:07:43,087
You've got until tomorrow, anyway.
Think you're good enough to take me on?

152
00:07:43,171 --> 00:07:45,214
Maybe we'll have to give you a head start.

153
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:46,591
Maybe. [laughs]

154
00:07:47,675 --> 00:07:48,885
We'll see what you got.

155
00:07:52,096 --> 00:07:53,806
With me being total shit out there,

156
00:07:53,890 --> 00:07:56,601
I can't imagine you hate me
any less than the others?

157
00:07:56,684 --> 00:07:58,102
I don't hate you.

158
00:07:58,936 --> 00:07:59,937
But you were shit.

159
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:01,981
Yeah, that was rough.

160
00:08:02,064 --> 00:08:04,650
-And the guys do not pull any punches.
-Yeah.

161
00:08:05,151 --> 00:08:07,945
No one's going to go easy on you.
You swim or you sink.

162
00:08:08,029 --> 00:08:10,114
I have to, or I can't keep training.

163
00:08:10,198 --> 00:08:13,075
Can you give me any insight
into these guys?

164
00:08:13,159 --> 00:08:15,912
Apparently to cox them,
you need to understand them.

165
00:08:15,995 --> 00:08:17,330
[intriguing music playing]

166
00:08:17,413 --> 00:08:18,623
Josh Regis.

167
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:20,833
The boy who would be king.

168
00:08:20,917 --> 00:08:24,420
[Cam] His dad won four Haverford Cups
as stroke seat. Josh can't compete.

169
00:08:25,004 --> 00:08:25,922
Next.

170
00:08:26,005 --> 00:08:29,133
Josh's cousin Ryder.
He's less of an heir, more of a spare.

171
00:08:29,217 --> 00:08:31,260
Baloo, real name Bronson.

172
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:34,138
He's the heart of the engine room
and crumbles under pressure.

173
00:08:34,222 --> 00:08:36,933
He should be nowhere near eight seat.
Mom's a senator.

174
00:08:37,016 --> 00:08:40,269
-Wait, is he Britney's brother?
-Twibling.

175
00:08:41,479 --> 00:08:45,358
Their mom used two different surrogates
at the same time. Designer twins.

176
00:08:45,441 --> 00:08:49,403
Wow, whoa. What is with this school?

177
00:08:49,487 --> 00:08:54,575
Your four seat is our powerhouse.
Damon Quaid. New guy from the second boat.

178
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:57,620
Bit of a troublemaker,
as opposed to Noah Bainbridge.

179
00:08:57,703 --> 00:09:00,706
-Cultured and refined, i.e. boring.
-[Noah] All of it.

180
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:03,042
But he takes rowing seriously
and expects everyone else to.

181
00:09:04,418 --> 00:09:08,256
Perry Chou.
Always on trend, never on rhythm.

182
00:09:08,339 --> 00:09:10,216
And Chris, a.k.a. Crabcatcher.

183
00:09:10,299 --> 00:09:13,010
From the junior boat.
The nickname explains itself.

184
00:09:13,094 --> 00:09:14,387
Thanks.

185
00:09:15,096 --> 00:09:21,185
And you? Cam Dillinger. Lone wolf.
Only has eyes for the next clean catch.

186
00:09:21,269 --> 00:09:22,770
[both laughing]

187
00:09:22,853 --> 00:09:23,938
Yeah, pretty much.

188
00:09:24,021 --> 00:09:26,899
All right. Enough chatter.
Let's hit the showers.

189
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:30,069
Teagan, your change room's down the hall.
Grab your things.

190
00:09:32,947 --> 00:09:36,951
My cox box! Who did…? Di…

191
00:09:40,621 --> 00:09:42,582
-Who's that?
-Ha, ha.

192
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:44,417
[Hayden] That is our new coxswain.

193
00:09:46,294 --> 00:09:47,712
What happened to Liam?

194
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:53,718
-Well, how much experience does she have?
-Oh, lots.

195
00:09:53,801 --> 00:09:55,595
She had her first practice today.

196
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:57,930
How's my son
supposed to lead the team with her?

197
00:09:58,014 --> 00:10:01,350
Well, see, he doesn't have that problem.

198
00:10:01,892 --> 00:10:03,144
Because he's not in stroke.

199
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:07,315
Okay, boys, listen up.

200
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:12,862
We need to win tomorrow, all right?

201
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:16,282
I'll talk to Coach and get back
in the eight. It's not up for discussion.

202
00:10:16,782 --> 00:10:19,869
Yeah, if you wanna think inside the box.

203
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:23,247
Or… you could try me.

204
00:10:23,873 --> 00:10:26,626
-Or me.
-Or the person with the best technique.

205
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:28,711
-And who's that?
-It's Cam.

206
00:10:28,794 --> 00:10:29,670
[scoffs]

207
00:10:30,171 --> 00:10:31,422
It's not Cam.

208
00:10:33,049 --> 00:10:37,094
Cam's bladework is impeccable,
and he gets the most out of the boat.

209
00:10:37,178 --> 00:10:39,055
He should get a shot.

210
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:40,640
[door slams]

211
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:44,810
[intriguing music playing]

212
00:10:46,228 --> 00:10:49,273
[boys arguing indistinctly]

213
00:10:51,567 --> 00:10:52,610
Ugh.

214
00:10:52,693 --> 00:10:56,489
[muffled arguing, water running]

215
00:10:56,572 --> 00:10:59,325
[Perry] Ryder's right.
We need fresh blood in stroke.

216
00:11:02,662 --> 00:11:04,038
That's funny.

217
00:11:04,705 --> 00:11:06,582
Hey, we don't have to argue.

218
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:11,128
Show of hands, who thinks
Perry should get a shot at stroke?

219
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:16,592
Wow, thanks, guys.

220
00:11:16,676 --> 00:11:18,594
[Ryder] Dude,
you're not as good as your dad.

221
00:11:19,136 --> 00:11:20,805
Anyone for Cam?

222
00:11:22,890 --> 00:11:25,476
Didn't think so. And how about Ryder?

223
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:29,814
And that's two.

224
00:11:32,024 --> 00:11:33,693
And who thinks it should be me?

225
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:37,988
-Whoa!
-Whoa!

226
00:11:38,072 --> 00:11:39,198
-[all clamoring]
-Ooh…

227
00:11:39,281 --> 00:11:40,950
-Uh, sorry.
-What the hell?

228
00:11:41,033 --> 00:11:42,493
What are you doing?

229
00:11:42,576 --> 00:11:46,163
-I'm on the team. Don't I get a vote?
-Everyone knows who you're voting for.

230
00:11:46,831 --> 00:11:49,125
All right, who's backing me?

231
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:57,007
-Then it's settled by popular vote.
-Yeah, except it's Coach's decision.

232
00:11:57,091 --> 00:11:58,968
[Teagan] Exactly. Thank you.

233
00:11:59,927 --> 00:12:03,472
-Can you get out of here?
-Yep. I am… Oh!

234
00:12:03,556 --> 00:12:06,100
Sorry, Noah, I was not expecting that.

235
00:12:06,934 --> 00:12:08,644
This cannot be the new normal.

236
00:12:08,728 --> 00:12:09,854
[door closes]

237
00:12:11,647 --> 00:12:13,566
[Teagan] Why are we going
to parents' night?

238
00:12:13,649 --> 00:12:15,151
[Ella] We need to impress the families

239
00:12:15,234 --> 00:12:18,195
so you can get a scholarship
and you don't get kicked out.

240
00:12:18,696 --> 00:12:20,156
Recognize anyone?

241
00:12:20,906 --> 00:12:22,408
I think saw my English teacher.

242
00:12:22,491 --> 00:12:25,244
Waste of time. How hard can English be?

243
00:12:25,327 --> 00:12:26,912
We have to find wealthy families

244
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:28,998
who'll think of you
when they're bequeathing.

245
00:12:29,081 --> 00:12:31,709
[modern string quartet music playing]

246
00:12:31,792 --> 00:12:34,712
Beautiful space, isn't it?

247
00:12:34,795 --> 00:12:37,006
-My father donated it.
-[gasps]

248
00:12:37,089 --> 00:12:38,883
Handpicked every piece of furniture.

249
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:40,468
Oh my gosh.

250
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:42,553
Gwendolyn Chou.

251
00:12:43,053 --> 00:12:45,347
-I'm Ella. This is my daughter, Teagan.
-Hi.

252
00:12:45,431 --> 00:12:46,682
Hi.

253
00:12:46,766 --> 00:12:47,725
Ah.

254
00:12:47,808 --> 00:12:50,936
The new coxswain.
I've heard about you from my son, Perry,

255
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:54,690
which means
you must be the wife of that… hotelier.

256
00:12:54,774 --> 00:12:56,609
[Teagan, quietly] Abort, abort.

257
00:12:56,692 --> 00:12:57,526
You know what?

258
00:12:57,610 --> 00:13:00,529
-Wife can be a loose association.
-Would you excuse me?

259
00:13:06,577 --> 00:13:08,537
[clears throat] Nice group of people.

260
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:11,081
Well, we tried.

261
00:13:13,667 --> 00:13:15,503
[Hayden] How long do we have to be here?

262
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:17,171
[Lana] Just a couple of hours.

263
00:13:17,254 --> 00:13:19,089
Goddamn parents' night.

264
00:13:19,173 --> 00:13:20,674
You are so dramatic.

265
00:13:20,758 --> 00:13:22,259
They're a bunch of hyenas.

266
00:13:22,343 --> 00:13:24,428
-All these Karens.
-Hey!

267
00:13:24,512 --> 00:13:26,806
What? It's a gender-neutral term.

268
00:13:27,306 --> 00:13:29,433
They just think I'm for sale,
which I'm not.

269
00:13:29,517 --> 00:13:31,769
You are overreacting. It's gonna be fine.

270
00:13:31,852 --> 00:13:33,020
[woman] Coach Hayden.

271
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:37,024
I would love to chat with you about Ryder.

272
00:13:37,107 --> 00:13:38,067
See?

273
00:13:38,567 --> 00:13:39,777
-Bye.
-Hey!

274
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:42,863
His summer rowing coach
said he was going to make a call

275
00:13:42,947 --> 00:13:44,490
-to the national team…
-Thank you.

276
00:13:44,573 --> 00:13:46,617
…to put Ryder on his radar.

277
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:51,121
-I can see why. Ryder's doing well.
-I understand you're changing up stroke.

278
00:13:51,205 --> 00:13:52,665
We're keeping our options open.

279
00:13:53,165 --> 00:13:55,042
Of course. Oh, um…

280
00:13:55,125 --> 00:13:58,420
Ryder mentioned
that some of the ergs need repair.

281
00:13:58,504 --> 00:14:00,422
Would a new set help you out?

282
00:14:00,506 --> 00:14:04,134
You know what? That's a generous offer,
but I'd have to run it by admin first.

283
00:14:04,218 --> 00:14:05,219
Yeah.

284
00:14:05,302 --> 00:14:07,429
-You enjoy your night. Yeah.
-Thank you.

285
00:14:08,180 --> 00:14:10,474
[Hayden sighs] Goddamn parents' night.

286
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:15,813
So how is it that you're not in stroke?

287
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:20,192
Coach has been "experimenting."
It's only temporary.

288
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:22,862
It's an embarrassment, is what it is.

289
00:14:23,362 --> 00:14:24,488
I'll get it back.

290
00:14:24,989 --> 00:14:27,157
No. I will.

291
00:14:28,534 --> 00:14:29,535
Where's Hayden?

292
00:14:31,078 --> 00:14:33,414
Hi…

293
00:14:33,497 --> 00:14:34,582
[laughing] Oh wow.

294
00:14:35,082 --> 00:14:37,001
Okay, that was just ugly.

295
00:14:38,377 --> 00:14:39,378
Ah…

296
00:14:41,422 --> 00:14:42,923
-Here you go.
-[whispers] Thank you.

297
00:14:44,884 --> 00:14:46,552
Teagan. Teagan's mom.

298
00:14:46,635 --> 00:14:47,636
Ella.

299
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:50,055
Wanna sign up
for our parents' association?

300
00:14:50,139 --> 00:14:51,932
-Mm-mm-mm.
-Oh.

301
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:53,767
-No, thank you.
-Um, where have you been?

302
00:14:53,851 --> 00:14:57,354
I was gated. It's like house arrest,
but the school is my house.

303
00:14:57,438 --> 00:14:59,148
Cabrera also has me working tonight.

304
00:14:59,231 --> 00:15:03,152
Ella, you look hot.
Not like the drab moms.

305
00:15:03,235 --> 00:15:06,947
Thank you. Not that it's helping
our cred in this room.

306
00:15:07,031 --> 00:15:10,242
Yeah, it turns out fancy people
don't love it when your dad's a felon.

307
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:13,203
These Eagle's Cove elite
actually love a scandal.

308
00:15:13,287 --> 00:15:15,122
Helps them feel better about themselves.

309
00:15:15,205 --> 00:15:19,835
If that's true,
then… any attention is good attention.

310
00:15:20,461 --> 00:15:22,546
-[Juliet] Hm?
-Anybody seen the bar?

311
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:23,505
Huh.

312
00:15:27,134 --> 00:15:28,886
-What's up, dude?
-Hey, man.

313
00:15:28,969 --> 00:15:31,513
-How's it going?
-Good.

314
00:15:31,597 --> 00:15:32,890
You guys just get here?

315
00:15:33,849 --> 00:15:37,061
-Yeah, we did.
-What's the deal with Josh and Ryder?

316
00:15:37,144 --> 00:15:39,730
Oh, talk about scandals.

317
00:15:39,813 --> 00:15:42,775
Josh's dad was the only heir
to the Regis empire,

318
00:15:42,858 --> 00:15:46,779
and then it came out that his father
had an affair with the dog walker

319
00:15:46,862 --> 00:15:49,657
and had a secret love child, Ryder's mom.

320
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:50,699
[Teagan] No way.

321
00:15:50,783 --> 00:15:54,078
Josh and Ryder get along,
but, well, rumor is,

322
00:15:54,161 --> 00:16:00,250
Josh's side of the Regis family
call Ryder's side the Egregiouses.

323
00:16:02,169 --> 00:16:03,420
Yeah, so…

324
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:08,217
I haven't needed to drink this bad
since the FBI raided my house.

325
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:10,678
[gasps] The FBI raided your house?

326
00:16:10,761 --> 00:16:12,221
It was horrible.

327
00:16:12,304 --> 00:16:15,265
They tore through the house,
ruined the carpet,

328
00:16:15,349 --> 00:16:16,684
and they took all my Birkins.

329
00:16:16,767 --> 00:16:19,144
[gasps] I would've had
a breakdown right there.

330
00:16:19,228 --> 00:16:21,397
I need more Chardonnay
just thinking about it.

331
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,898
-[gasps]
-[giggling]

332
00:16:22,982 --> 00:16:24,441
[Ella] If you'll excuse me.

333
00:16:33,117 --> 00:16:34,785
Not bad.

334
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:36,495
Hm?

335
00:16:36,578 --> 00:16:40,582
The Easton moms.
You got them hanging on your every word.

336
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:42,376
Well played.

337
00:16:42,876 --> 00:16:44,837
I don't think we've met.

338
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:47,339
We haven't. I'm Imogen.

339
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:50,759
So you're the woman whose husband
ripped everyone off and is now on the lam.

340
00:16:50,843 --> 00:16:51,969
Ah.

341
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:54,096
Yeah.

342
00:16:54,847 --> 00:16:57,224
Still less dysfunctional than mine.

343
00:16:57,307 --> 00:16:58,350
[chuckles]

344
00:16:59,727 --> 00:17:02,312
The sins of the husband
do not fall on the wife.

345
00:17:03,063 --> 00:17:04,857
Welcome to the Easton circus.

346
00:17:10,904 --> 00:17:13,073
-I should get back to my daughter.
-You should.

347
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:14,491
And by the way, this?

348
00:17:15,576 --> 00:17:16,744
Don't change a thing.

349
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:25,377
Hi.

350
00:17:25,461 --> 00:17:28,505
Did you just scandalize
your way into a scholarship?

351
00:17:29,173 --> 00:17:33,052
I don't know,
but I think I've made a new friend.

352
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:37,181
Thank you.

353
00:17:38,682 --> 00:17:40,309
-Have you seen Hayden?
-Mm.

354
00:17:40,392 --> 00:17:41,477
Inside.

355
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:44,813
He's gone.

356
00:17:46,398 --> 00:17:47,649
Thank you.

357
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:50,277
Better decide stroke seat
before they start hunting in packs.

358
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:53,447
Ugh. I've been offered everything
from a board seat at a tech start-up

359
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:56,158
to, I think, sexual favors.

360
00:17:56,241 --> 00:17:58,243
Hm. Well, how lonely are you?

361
00:17:58,952 --> 00:17:59,828
Mm.

362
00:17:59,912 --> 00:18:02,664
[laughs] Seriously, though,
who's it gonna be?

363
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:05,209
I dunno.
I think I've got to take a chance.

364
00:18:05,292 --> 00:18:07,628
Easton parents be damned.

365
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,588
Hey, Cam.

366
00:18:12,758 --> 00:18:14,218
Coach, have you been hiding?

367
00:18:16,136 --> 00:18:18,388
It's you. You're stroke.

368
00:18:19,264 --> 00:18:20,265
Seriously?

369
00:18:21,517 --> 00:18:22,601
You've earned it.

370
00:18:24,019 --> 00:18:25,145
[laughs]

371
00:18:26,021 --> 00:18:27,272
Thanks, Coach.

372
00:18:31,068 --> 00:18:33,987
-[Richard] There you are.
-I've been meaning to catch up with you.

373
00:18:34,071 --> 00:18:37,116
Look, I understand you're on
some sort of "everyone gets a turn" kick,

374
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:40,160
but enough's enough. You have
a tried-and-true stroke seat here.

375
00:18:40,244 --> 00:18:43,247
I've made my decision.
You'll see it on the boat.

376
00:18:48,001 --> 00:18:50,879
-Coach. Thanks.
-Well, I am very…

377
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:54,216
Dad, look. I think we know who he picked.

378
00:18:54,299 --> 00:18:55,384
It's gonna be good.

379
00:18:56,927 --> 00:18:58,470
We'll see about that.

380
00:19:01,098 --> 00:19:06,728
[upbeat music playing]

381
00:19:08,438 --> 00:19:09,523
You nervous?

382
00:19:10,023 --> 00:19:13,235
Course not. It's only if I lose this,
I'll get kicked off the team,

383
00:19:13,318 --> 00:19:15,320
and my rowing career will be over.

384
00:19:16,446 --> 00:19:19,116
Wow, is it Bring Your Dad to Row Day?

385
00:19:20,534 --> 00:19:22,452
Your dad's never missed a race.

386
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:26,081
-It's fine. I wouldn't want him here.
-Well, no.

387
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:29,042
But I bet you'd want that In-N-Out Burger
he always brought you.

388
00:19:29,126 --> 00:19:32,588
-Mm.
-Hey, new pregame tradition.

389
00:19:32,671 --> 00:19:34,256
-Let's go.
-What?

390
00:19:34,923 --> 00:19:37,009
[soft music playing]

391
00:19:37,634 --> 00:19:39,970
[Ella] It's a quiet spot, not far.

392
00:19:40,512 --> 00:19:42,472
Growing up,
I used to come here with a friend.

393
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:45,184
An Easton rower, actually.

394
00:19:45,684 --> 00:19:47,394
[loon calling]

395
00:19:47,477 --> 00:19:50,981
Always thought this place
was kind of magical. Don't laugh.

396
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:54,067
[chuckles] I'm not. I like it.

397
00:19:54,151 --> 00:19:58,280
I know your dad would have some kind of
pep talk for you for race day.

398
00:19:58,363 --> 00:20:02,868
I'm sorry I don't have anything,
but be fast and don't fall in.

399
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:05,245
-That's good.
-[announcer] <i>Attendees.</i>

400
00:20:05,329 --> 00:20:08,332
<i>-The alumni race will begin in 30 minutes.</i>
-Okay, I gotta go.

401
00:20:08,415 --> 00:20:09,374
Okay.

402
00:20:09,917 --> 00:20:12,377
All right. Break a leg or an oar.

403
00:20:14,171 --> 00:20:17,382
Hey, there's been a change in plans,
but I will make it up to you.

404
00:20:18,592 --> 00:20:20,052
Okay, listen up.

405
00:20:22,888 --> 00:20:24,681
Josh, you're back in stroke.

406
00:20:24,765 --> 00:20:26,183
-Oh…
-[Hayden] Cam in seven.

407
00:20:26,266 --> 00:20:28,310
-Then Baloo, Quaid, and Ryder.
-[rower] Nice.

408
00:20:28,393 --> 00:20:31,313
Clean catches, and remember
to use the full length of the stroke,

409
00:20:31,396 --> 00:20:33,440
because if you do not,
we will whoop your ass.

410
00:20:33,523 --> 00:20:35,567
[all exclaiming]

411
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,819
See you out on the water.

412
00:20:37,903 --> 00:20:39,613
Let's go. Hustle.

413
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:46,495
It was out of my hands.

414
00:20:46,578 --> 00:20:48,830
Not like a coach'd
make decisions for his boat.

415
00:20:48,914 --> 00:20:52,417
Look, I get it, all right?
I rowed with Josh's dad. It's not fair.

416
00:20:52,501 --> 00:20:55,045
I'm a better rower. I deserve it.

417
00:20:55,128 --> 00:20:56,296
Yeah, but so did I.

418
00:20:56,797 --> 00:20:59,299
Easton wants to see
a certain person in stroke.

419
00:20:59,383 --> 00:21:02,928
They don't want a townie. They want
someone the Easton crowd can follow.

420
00:21:03,011 --> 00:21:04,429
So, not us.

421
00:21:06,473 --> 00:21:07,474
[Cam exhales]

422
00:21:08,725 --> 00:21:10,769
I'm going to the Olympics one day, Coach.

423
00:21:11,645 --> 00:21:12,729
Do you think Josh is?

424
00:21:12,813 --> 00:21:17,776
[tense music playing]

425
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:26,076
Don't screw this up.
I got a lot riding on this.

426
00:21:26,159 --> 00:21:27,494
I won't if you won't.

427
00:21:30,372 --> 00:21:31,999
Two minutes to launch!

428
00:21:32,082 --> 00:21:34,584
So what if your dads
won the Haverford Cup?

429
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:36,503
[Richard] All eight, watch descent.

430
00:21:44,803 --> 00:21:49,349
Over head! Hands across! Roll it in!

431
00:21:50,892 --> 00:21:54,021
Right foot in! Lean!

432
00:21:54,104 --> 00:21:58,025
On jump! One, two, jump!

433
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:02,696
Lean!

434
00:22:02,779 --> 00:22:03,947
Are we screwed?

435
00:22:05,032 --> 00:22:06,241
[Perry] Big time.

436
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:12,205
[Teagan] Okay. [clears throat]

437
00:22:13,707 --> 00:22:16,001
I was thinking we start with a sprint,

438
00:22:16,626 --> 00:22:19,171
drop down, then back up
for the last 500 meters.

439
00:22:20,672 --> 00:22:23,550
It's actually not a bad idea.
Let's try it.

440
00:22:24,051 --> 00:22:28,013
[intense dance music playing]

441
00:22:31,725 --> 00:22:33,894
-Ready… row!
-[horn blows]

442
00:22:33,977 --> 00:22:38,398
-[Teagan] Steady. Give me five.
-[cox] Long and strong.

443
00:22:38,482 --> 00:22:40,400
[Teagan] Four.

444
00:22:40,484 --> 00:22:43,570
-Three.
-[cox] Okay, boys, find our rhythm.

445
00:22:43,653 --> 00:22:48,200
[Teagan] All right, looking good here.
Pull up the rate. Let's give it a sprint.

446
00:22:48,283 --> 00:22:50,118
[intense music continues]

447
00:22:54,998 --> 00:22:56,958
Good work! We're pulling ahead!

448
00:23:00,212 --> 00:23:04,257
Okay, let's take it down two beats.
Do it together.

449
00:23:05,384 --> 00:23:06,676
Bring back!

450
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:08,720
Make it count. Come on!

451
00:23:08,804 --> 00:23:10,347
[cox] Pick up the rate.

452
00:23:11,973 --> 00:23:13,350
[Teagan] Win!

453
00:23:15,310 --> 00:23:17,604
[cox] Close the gap. Sharp.

454
00:23:17,687 --> 00:23:19,356
-Sharp!
-Hey, let's go earlier!

455
00:23:19,439 --> 00:23:22,025
-Not yet. They'll get scrambly!
-I wanna go now!

456
00:23:22,109 --> 00:23:24,611
Wait for my call! Don't push!

457
00:23:24,694 --> 00:23:26,822
[Josh] I'm going! Pick it up, boys!

458
00:23:26,905 --> 00:23:27,948
[Teagan] Josh!

459
00:23:28,448 --> 00:23:30,158
You're off rhythm. Take it easy!

460
00:23:30,242 --> 00:23:32,160
-[Quaid] Hey, wait up!
-See?

461
00:23:32,244 --> 00:23:33,495
[Noah] We're getting smoked.

462
00:23:33,578 --> 00:23:35,455
-Starboard needs power.
-[Crabcatcher] I can't keep up!

463
00:23:35,539 --> 00:23:38,166
[Teagan] I told you they'd get scrambly.
Now we're way behind.

464
00:23:38,750 --> 00:23:41,503
-Pull!
-[cox] The end's in sight.

465
00:23:41,586 --> 00:23:43,630
Let's send it. One.

466
00:23:44,798 --> 00:23:46,007
-Two.
-Go, go now!

467
00:23:47,467 --> 00:23:52,264
Legs! You want to lose to your dads? Pull!

468
00:23:55,016 --> 00:23:55,851
[horn blows]

469
00:23:56,893 --> 00:23:57,936
[boys groaning]

470
00:23:58,019 --> 00:23:59,855
-[Perry] Ugh, come on.
-[man] Eagle pride!

471
00:23:59,938 --> 00:24:01,148
Yeah!

472
00:24:01,231 --> 00:24:03,066
[men cheering]

473
00:24:03,150 --> 00:24:04,234
Ugh!

474
00:24:04,776 --> 00:24:07,028
-[men cheering and laughing]
-[cox] Told you!

475
00:24:08,029 --> 00:24:08,947
Good guys!

476
00:24:12,617 --> 00:24:13,618
You should've called.

477
00:24:14,369 --> 00:24:15,996
You should've waited.

478
00:24:20,208 --> 00:24:25,380
[indie music playing]

479
00:24:26,298 --> 00:24:31,636
<i>♪ Woke up every day</i>
<i>And I can feel it's always here ♪</i>

480
00:24:34,264 --> 00:24:35,348
[Richard laughing]

481
00:24:37,017 --> 00:24:38,685
Looking good, crew.

482
00:24:39,186 --> 00:24:43,356
Nothing like tradition, hm?
Losers serve the winners.

483
00:24:44,441 --> 00:24:46,401
You'll get them next time.

484
00:24:48,945 --> 00:24:52,157
Oh, so stingy with the potato salad.

485
00:24:53,658 --> 00:24:54,493
That's better.

486
00:24:55,744 --> 00:24:58,246
-[Britney] Mm, no fish for me.
-[Richard] Keep it coming.

487
00:24:58,330 --> 00:25:00,999
Maybe next time
you'll actually listen to me.

488
00:25:01,082 --> 00:25:03,919
[scoffs] Like you weren't
rushing the slide.

489
00:25:04,419 --> 00:25:05,754
She's not wrong.

490
00:25:06,379 --> 00:25:07,756
Catches were shit.

491
00:25:07,839 --> 00:25:08,965
Excuse me?

492
00:25:13,428 --> 00:25:17,974
Look, you're shit at coxing,
and you know it. You should just quit.

493
00:25:18,475 --> 00:25:21,144
Lay off her. We had a bad race.
You don't have to cry about it.

494
00:25:22,103 --> 00:25:23,188
[utensil clatters]

495
00:25:24,481 --> 00:25:26,358
-Hey.
-[rower] Whoa.

496
00:25:29,778 --> 00:25:31,112
Thanks, uh…

497
00:25:31,196 --> 00:25:33,698
Though I can stand up for myself,
you know.

498
00:25:33,782 --> 00:25:36,284
Oh, I'm well aware.

499
00:25:38,495 --> 00:25:41,873
Maybe I should've listened to Josh.
At least we would've been in sync.

500
00:25:42,624 --> 00:25:44,834
You're not the first coxie
to fight with your stroke seat.

501
00:25:45,460 --> 00:25:46,461
Let it go.

502
00:25:48,797 --> 00:25:50,298
It should've been you.

503
00:25:52,300 --> 00:25:55,262
-Well, I guess Coach felt otherwise.
-Well, he's wrong.

504
00:26:01,393 --> 00:26:03,520
Ugh, potato salad.

505
00:26:03,603 --> 00:26:06,856
You shouldn't have eaten so much, doofus.
Iron Crucible in the morning.

506
00:26:06,940 --> 00:26:08,900
It's not that bad, is it?

507
00:26:12,612 --> 00:26:16,241
-Hey! Hi, Bronson.
-Hello.

508
00:26:16,324 --> 00:26:19,202
So, um,
we need to talk about that pull pic.

509
00:26:19,703 --> 00:26:22,205
It's cringe,
and you're going to embarrass Mom.

510
00:26:22,706 --> 00:26:25,375
Why? Is there something on my face?

511
00:26:25,458 --> 00:26:26,293
Uh…

512
00:26:28,086 --> 00:26:30,422
It's a tad… thirsty.

513
00:26:30,505 --> 00:26:31,381
[laughs]

514
00:26:32,048 --> 00:26:33,049
Okay.

515
00:26:33,758 --> 00:26:35,468
You found your man. Let me find mine.

516
00:26:35,552 --> 00:26:37,137
She's got elections coming up.

517
00:26:37,220 --> 00:26:39,514
If Mom has a problem with it,
she'll say something.

518
00:26:39,598 --> 00:26:42,851
But she won't,
because look how cute I am in this. Oh.

519
00:26:42,934 --> 00:26:43,935
[Britney laughs]

520
00:26:45,103 --> 00:26:46,938
-[Baloo] Who is this?
-[Britney] Oh.

521
00:26:49,941 --> 00:26:52,235
Okay. So he's hot. Whatever.

522
00:26:52,319 --> 00:26:54,237
See, there's a method to my madness.

523
00:26:59,326 --> 00:27:00,910
[Britney] If you're doing HIIT workouts…

524
00:27:00,994 --> 00:27:03,038
Everyone! A few words.

525
00:27:03,997 --> 00:27:06,458
[indistinct chatter]

526
00:27:07,459 --> 00:27:08,710
To my fellow alumni.

527
00:27:09,210 --> 00:27:11,463
-Eagle pride!
-[alumni] Eagle pride!

528
00:27:11,546 --> 00:27:15,967
We've got a big season ahead of us.
This is the year we commit to each other.

529
00:27:16,051 --> 00:27:19,596
-The year we…
-…take down Westvale, huh? Hm?

530
00:27:19,679 --> 00:27:20,722
[alumni cheering]

531
00:27:20,805 --> 00:27:22,599
Whoo, yeah!

532
00:27:23,099 --> 00:27:24,934
[all clapping and cheering]

533
00:27:25,018 --> 00:27:28,605
All right. Everybody have fun tonight,
but remember, don't stay up too late.

534
00:27:28,688 --> 00:27:30,565
We've got the Crucible in the morning.

535
00:27:31,191 --> 00:27:32,192
Carry on.

536
00:27:34,527 --> 00:27:36,821
It's not exactly
the message I was going for.

537
00:27:36,905 --> 00:27:39,032
Competition needs
a little bloodlust, Hayden.

538
00:27:39,115 --> 00:27:41,368
You never liked that though.
It's part of the way you coach.

539
00:27:41,451 --> 00:27:43,995
Josh is in the stroke. You had your say.

540
00:27:44,496 --> 00:27:46,122
What'd it take, by the way?

541
00:27:46,206 --> 00:27:49,751
Oh, uh, Principal Cabrera's niece
wanted an internship at Louis Vuitton.

542
00:27:49,834 --> 00:27:54,047
Yeah. I made a call.
I want to win, man. Don't you?

543
00:27:55,048 --> 00:27:57,258
-You can't buy a championship.
-Mm…

544
00:27:57,342 --> 00:28:01,304
The sooner these guys understand that,
the sooner we'll get back to winning.

545
00:28:04,224 --> 00:28:07,394
[tense music playing]

546
00:28:07,477 --> 00:28:08,395
[exhales]

547
00:28:14,317 --> 00:28:15,902
Nothing appealing?

548
00:28:16,444 --> 00:28:18,738
Ah, I just finished
a three-hour lunch rush

549
00:28:18,822 --> 00:28:22,200
serving clams, mussels, and scallops. So…

550
00:28:22,283 --> 00:28:23,952
-You're mollusked out.
-Yeah.

551
00:28:24,452 --> 00:28:27,914
Hot tip. I tried some of that apricot jam
from the dessert with the kielbasa.

552
00:28:27,997 --> 00:28:28,832
Hm.

553
00:28:32,502 --> 00:28:34,713
Mm… Mm!

554
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:36,548
Where did you learn that?

555
00:28:36,631 --> 00:28:39,676
My husband owned
a chain of boutique hotels.

556
00:28:39,759 --> 00:28:42,512
-We had weddings and galas.
-You're an event planner.

557
00:28:42,595 --> 00:28:45,640
Not officially.
I'm just, like, the wife of the boss.

558
00:28:45,724 --> 00:28:50,520
But clients liked my ideas, and I liked
planning their parties with them.

559
00:28:50,603 --> 00:28:52,522
Your husband had money,
but you had the taste.

560
00:28:52,605 --> 00:28:54,441
Turns out he didn't even have the money,

561
00:28:54,524 --> 00:28:55,608
-so…
-[laughs]

562
00:28:56,109 --> 00:28:59,821
Finding new party themes is hard.
I mean, everything is so overdone.

563
00:28:59,904 --> 00:29:04,659
The trick is to find something
that's as unique as the client is.

564
00:29:04,743 --> 00:29:05,577
Mm.

565
00:29:06,536 --> 00:29:08,580
Like apricot kielbasa.

566
00:29:10,165 --> 00:29:12,167
Are you busy two Saturdays from now?

567
00:29:13,084 --> 00:29:15,253
James Bond-inspired casino night.
Do you wanna come?

568
00:29:15,336 --> 00:29:19,632
Talk about things being overdone.
License to snooze, right?

569
00:29:21,176 --> 00:29:22,343
It's actually my party.

570
00:29:22,427 --> 00:29:24,387
-Oh.
-For my son's birthday.

571
00:29:25,305 --> 00:29:26,973
He's a big Bond fan.

572
00:29:27,056 --> 00:29:28,600
-Yeah.
-Okay.

573
00:29:28,683 --> 00:29:31,728
Ah. Forgive me. I get verbal blah.

574
00:29:32,562 --> 00:29:35,899
When I'm tired, or any time, actually.

575
00:29:37,150 --> 00:29:39,402
-Wanna tell me about the party?
-Oh, maybe another time.

576
00:29:43,490 --> 00:29:44,491
[grunts]

577
00:29:45,658 --> 00:29:46,743
Josh.

578
00:29:49,037 --> 00:29:52,415
My first alumni race,
I lost to your grandfather.

579
00:29:53,208 --> 00:29:55,001
It's a rite of passage.

580
00:29:56,002 --> 00:30:00,882
That anger you feel, that fire,
that's the fuel you need to win.

581
00:30:03,134 --> 00:30:05,720
[emotional music playing]

582
00:30:05,804 --> 00:30:09,224
My second race,
I beat him by a boat length.

583
00:30:09,307 --> 00:30:10,225
[laughs]

584
00:30:10,809 --> 00:30:12,185
You'll get us next year.

585
00:30:14,354 --> 00:30:16,105
I expect nothing less.

586
00:30:16,731 --> 00:30:19,651
[ominous music playing]

587
00:30:25,156 --> 00:30:26,783
[Ella] Matt Hayden?

588
00:30:28,827 --> 00:30:29,953
[laughs]

589
00:30:30,036 --> 00:30:31,746
I heard you were back in town.

590
00:30:32,247 --> 00:30:34,249
And yet no gift basket.

591
00:30:35,208 --> 00:30:37,669
That was wrong of me. I will do better?

592
00:30:37,752 --> 00:30:38,753
[Ella laughs]

593
00:30:40,880 --> 00:30:42,215
[Ella] Still come here, huh?

594
00:30:42,715 --> 00:30:45,385
Someone had to hold down the fort
for the last 20 years.

595
00:30:45,468 --> 00:30:47,470
You can't leave a view like this
unlooked at.

596
00:30:48,054 --> 00:30:49,514
Well, thanks for your service.

597
00:30:50,223 --> 00:30:51,474
My pleasure. [chuckles]

598
00:30:53,852 --> 00:30:55,520
-How you been?
-Ah.

599
00:30:56,187 --> 00:30:57,397
That's the question.

600
00:30:59,274 --> 00:31:03,278
Wait, you really don't know.
You didn't even think to google me?

601
00:31:03,778 --> 00:31:06,406
-I'm… sad?
-I'm not a screen guy.

602
00:31:06,489 --> 00:31:09,284
Not like my daughter, Madison,
who you'll meet sometime.

603
00:31:09,367 --> 00:31:11,911
She's a teen with a lot of opinions.

604
00:31:11,995 --> 00:31:14,497
-Teenagers are the worst.
-Yeah, the worst.

605
00:31:14,581 --> 00:31:16,457
-And it's just me.
-Mm.

606
00:31:16,541 --> 00:31:18,877
-Single parenting is impossible.
-Mm-hmm.

607
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:23,715
I just live in constant fear
that Teagan will hate me forever.

608
00:31:24,299 --> 00:31:26,259
Teagan's your daughter. Right.

609
00:31:26,342 --> 00:31:30,388
Of course. I should have known.
That bullheadedness came from somewhere.

610
00:31:31,306 --> 00:31:33,558
-Bullheaded? Me?
-[laughing]

611
00:31:34,058 --> 00:31:37,145
I never once managed to change your mind.

612
00:31:41,900 --> 00:31:43,109
I'm glad you're back.

613
00:31:43,985 --> 00:31:45,904
-You seem good.
-I'm a shell of a woman.

614
00:31:47,030 --> 00:31:48,406
Life is kicking my ass.

615
00:31:48,907 --> 00:31:49,949
Come on.

616
00:31:50,033 --> 00:31:55,246
You? The girl who got a second job
to buy a car to drive to her first?

617
00:31:57,165 --> 00:31:58,833
No, that girl knows how to survive.

618
00:32:00,919 --> 00:32:02,253
Remember that, huh?

619
00:32:03,546 --> 00:32:04,839
I remember all of it.

620
00:32:13,431 --> 00:32:14,432
Hey.

621
00:32:15,266 --> 00:32:17,435
A few of us are going for a dip.
You wanna come?

622
00:32:17,518 --> 00:32:21,397
[scoffs] No thanks, bruh.
You've been coming at me all day.

623
00:32:21,898 --> 00:32:24,692
What's the matter, your dad?
He get you all riled up?

624
00:32:25,401 --> 00:32:26,736
Don't talk to me about my family.

625
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:29,405
I'm a Regis too.

626
00:32:30,698 --> 00:32:32,241
Or is that not convenient for you today?

627
00:32:32,909 --> 00:32:34,369
I've always been there for you.

628
00:32:34,452 --> 00:32:36,704
Your dad is such a dick to you.

629
00:32:37,664 --> 00:32:38,957
And you just take it.

630
00:32:40,458 --> 00:32:41,459
Yeah?

631
00:32:42,085 --> 00:32:45,713
Well, your mom
is a grasping, status-hungry leech.

632
00:32:46,214 --> 00:32:47,757
How egregious.

633
00:32:48,383 --> 00:32:49,842
-[grunts]
-[rowers exclaiming]

634
00:32:49,926 --> 00:32:54,555
[aggressive rock music playing]

635
00:32:58,685 --> 00:32:59,852
Hey, stop!

636
00:33:02,522 --> 00:33:03,398
[Baloo] Oh, shit.

637
00:33:04,440 --> 00:33:05,984
[Cam] Guys. Guys, guys!

638
00:33:06,526 --> 00:33:07,735
Guys, we're teammates!

639
00:33:09,362 --> 00:33:10,738
[boy] Go, Ryder, go!

640
00:33:12,198 --> 00:33:13,700
Guys, break it up!

641
00:33:14,200 --> 00:33:16,244
[gasping]

642
00:33:18,162 --> 00:33:20,707
-[Cam] Josh. Josh, don't, don't!
-No, no, no, no, no! [screams]

643
00:33:22,875 --> 00:33:24,002
[exhales]

644
00:33:25,503 --> 00:33:26,462
[laughing] Oh.

645
00:33:26,546 --> 00:33:30,425
-You jackass!
-[yelling] Hey, you two! That's enough!

646
00:33:31,300 --> 00:33:34,804
What a disgrace!
Clambake's over! Crew, go home!

647
00:33:34,887 --> 00:33:38,516
And when I see you tomorrow,
I wanna see athletes, not children!

648
00:33:38,599 --> 00:33:39,892
You got me?

649
00:33:40,476 --> 00:33:41,477
Go!

650
00:33:41,561 --> 00:33:44,313
[quiet, tense music playing]

651
00:33:46,858 --> 00:33:48,901
[Cam] I don't think
I've ever seen Coach that mad.

652
00:33:48,985 --> 00:33:51,529
[Teagan] He can join
the rest of the crew who's pissed at me.

653
00:33:57,869 --> 00:33:58,911
[Cam exhales]

654
00:34:00,204 --> 00:34:01,706
See you tomorrow.

655
00:34:04,667 --> 00:34:09,797
Uh, I don't know, Cam. Look,
I don't think I'm right for this team.

656
00:34:09,881 --> 00:34:13,092
A team that wants to fight me
isn't going to follow me.

657
00:34:14,969 --> 00:34:18,389
That's too bad.
You're better than the last cox we had.

658
00:34:19,807 --> 00:34:21,517
Pisses off Josh so much.

659
00:34:24,562 --> 00:34:25,897
Yeah, it really does.

660
00:34:26,439 --> 00:34:27,565
[Teagan laughs softly]

661
00:34:29,233 --> 00:34:30,651
I hope I see you at the race.

662
00:34:30,735 --> 00:34:33,154
You're tough enough. They should know it.

663
00:34:47,043 --> 00:34:50,421
Are you sure about this?
It's 14 miles long.

664
00:34:50,505 --> 00:34:52,507
Yeah, I got this.

665
00:34:53,132 --> 00:34:55,468
[Cabrera] Welcome to the Iron Crucible!

666
00:34:56,385 --> 00:35:02,225
Easton Prep was founded on a mission
of unlocking every student's potential.

667
00:35:02,308 --> 00:35:09,232
Now, the purpose of the Iron Crucible
is not to finish, but to find your limits.

668
00:35:09,315 --> 00:35:12,068
And every year, to exceed them.

669
00:35:12,568 --> 00:35:14,821
Ready? Set…

670
00:35:15,822 --> 00:35:16,823
Race!

671
00:35:16,906 --> 00:35:18,491
["Run Rabbit" by Alt Blk Era playing]

672
00:35:18,574 --> 00:35:21,244
The course is comprised
of seven obstacles,

673
00:35:21,327 --> 00:35:24,413
each separated by a two-mile run.

674
00:35:24,497 --> 00:35:27,291
<i>♪ Run, rabbit, run, rabbit</i>
<i>Run, run, run ♪</i>

675
00:35:36,259 --> 00:35:39,428
Your wristbands let you check in
at each obstacle.

676
00:35:39,512 --> 00:35:40,596
[beeping]

677
00:35:43,307 --> 00:35:45,810
There's been a lot of bickering
about the stroke seat.

678
00:35:45,893 --> 00:35:48,104
So I'm going to make this fun.

679
00:35:48,187 --> 00:35:50,690
Whoever gets farthest wins stroke.

680
00:35:52,191 --> 00:35:55,903
<i>♪ …pulling me</i>
<i>Haven't had to run a mile since I was 17 ♪</i>

681
00:35:55,987 --> 00:35:58,281
[both grunting]

682
00:35:58,364 --> 00:36:01,534
<i>♪ Haven't had to tell myself</i>
<i>That you're a fever dream ♪</i>

683
00:36:01,617 --> 00:36:04,662
<i>♪'Cause you said to me</i>
<i>Do you wanna fall? Hold my hand ♪</i>

684
00:36:04,745 --> 00:36:05,788
[beeps]

685
00:36:05,872 --> 00:36:08,166
<i>♪ Why d'you wanna talk? Just run fast ♪</i>

686
00:36:08,249 --> 00:36:10,710
<i>♪ Don't you know it's all in your hands? ♪</i>

687
00:36:10,793 --> 00:36:13,421
<i>♪ Now you wanna crawl out my past ♪</i>

688
00:36:13,504 --> 00:36:14,839
<i>♪ Kicked out of the party ♪</i>

689
00:36:16,340 --> 00:36:18,759
<i>♪ And they said, "Run, rabbit</i>
<i>Run, rabbit, run, run, run" ♪</i>

690
00:36:18,843 --> 00:36:19,760
[beeping]

691
00:36:21,095 --> 00:36:22,388
<i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

692
00:36:22,889 --> 00:36:23,723
[groans]

693
00:36:23,806 --> 00:36:25,141
<i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

694
00:36:26,517 --> 00:36:27,685
<i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

695
00:36:29,312 --> 00:36:30,563
<i>♪ Run, run, run, rabbit ♪</i>

696
00:36:30,646 --> 00:36:32,899
Hey, do you know
where my kid is right now?

697
00:36:33,608 --> 00:36:35,193
They never tell you anything.

698
00:36:35,276 --> 00:36:38,029
You just have to wait
until your kid texts you that they're out.

699
00:36:38,905 --> 00:36:40,198
No one ever finishes?

700
00:36:40,281 --> 00:36:41,532
Some make it pretty far,

701
00:36:41,616 --> 00:36:44,952
but the last obstacle,
they hit the literal wall.

702
00:36:46,954 --> 00:36:50,750
Hey, look, I'm, uh, sorry
I was rude to you earlier.

703
00:36:51,709 --> 00:36:52,919
You weren't.

704
00:36:53,002 --> 00:36:55,630
You were being honest,
and I got huffy because you were right.

705
00:36:56,130 --> 00:36:58,216
Casino night has been done to death.

706
00:36:58,299 --> 00:37:01,135
It's a classic for a reason.
I'm sure it'll still be a good time.

707
00:37:01,219 --> 00:37:03,262
I want it to be better than good.

708
00:37:03,346 --> 00:37:06,974
I want it to be,
"thanks his mom on the Internet" good.

709
00:37:08,017 --> 00:37:09,894
It will be if I plan it.

710
00:37:11,187 --> 00:37:12,438
You? [laughs]

711
00:37:14,774 --> 00:37:16,776
You know what?
I think that's a great idea.

712
00:37:17,902 --> 00:37:21,072
So what's your usual budget?
100K and the fee is 15%?

713
00:37:21,572 --> 00:37:22,907
[laughs]

714
00:37:22,990 --> 00:37:23,991
Yes.

715
00:37:24,075 --> 00:37:25,493
-Yes?
-We can make that work.

716
00:37:25,576 --> 00:37:26,410
Okay.

717
00:37:26,494 --> 00:37:27,954
[both laughing]

718
00:37:28,037 --> 00:37:29,247
Ah!

719
00:37:29,330 --> 00:37:30,164
[beeping]

720
00:37:30,248 --> 00:37:31,082
[exhales]

721
00:37:31,165 --> 00:37:34,669
["I wanna See You Try"
by Apoena Ferreira Frota playing]

722
00:37:35,544 --> 00:37:37,171
[grunting]

723
00:37:38,506 --> 00:37:40,424
[grunting]

724
00:37:40,508 --> 00:37:41,717
[Baloo grunts]

725
00:37:44,262 --> 00:37:46,514
[both grunting and groaning]

726
00:37:47,932 --> 00:37:49,934
<i>♪ You want the power back ♪</i>

727
00:37:50,017 --> 00:37:51,769
<i>♪ I wanna see you try ♪</i>

728
00:37:51,852 --> 00:37:53,187
[Quaid moaning]

729
00:37:53,271 --> 00:37:54,480
[Teagan] You okay?

730
00:37:54,981 --> 00:37:56,023
<i>♪ Try ♪</i>

731
00:37:57,149 --> 00:37:58,526
<i>♪ I wanna see you try ♪</i>

732
00:37:58,609 --> 00:38:00,069
[Baloo] Come on, big boy.

733
00:38:00,611 --> 00:38:01,821
I'll bring him back.

734
00:38:02,530 --> 00:38:04,031
[Teagan] You don't wanna keep going?

735
00:38:08,244 --> 00:38:09,578
I didn't even want to start.

736
00:38:10,621 --> 00:38:14,750
<i>♪ Please don't make me laugh</i>
<i>I wanna see you try ♪</i>

737
00:38:15,418 --> 00:38:19,046
<i>♪ Anything that you can do</i>
